    <string name="info_message">IntentLab builds and sends intents and tests deep links on the phone.\n\nIdentity. Every intent is sent with the identity and permissions of IntentLab. It holds none beyond QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES, which is used to show which apps match. It claims no privileged access, so Android refuses what needs more.\n\nControl. Nothing is sent without your tap. IntentLab reads nothing from the intent that starts it, so another app cannot fill in this form. URI access is shown to you before it is granted.\n\nPrivacy. There is no Internet permission and no analytics. History stays in private storage and is left out of backups. Android itself can log activity starts in the system log.\n\nFree software under the GPL v3.</string>
